cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this repository, please cite it as below."
title: "Objective-aligned evaluation inflates the distributional gain in single-cell drug retrieval"
abstract: >-
  Code, analyses and manuscript sources for an audit of how distribution-aware
  single-cell drug retrieval is evaluated. Holding the candidate rankings, the
  scorer and the queries fixed and changing only the evaluating criterion, a
  distributional advantage that is large under a metric of its own kind is absent
  under a task-proximal mechanism criterion, and under an independent functional
  oracle is real but small, with almost all of what remains reproduced by a scalar
  that compares no distributions. The repository does not propose a better
  drug-ranking method: the population-to-population retrieval scores it implements
  are the instrument, released as JUDGE (Distributional Auditing of Retrieval
  Transfer). It also ships CORRECTIONS.md, a record of every number this project
  has retracted or revised.
authors:
  - name: "Boom5426"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Boom5426/JUDGE"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - single-cell
  - drug retrieval
  - distributional distance
  - perturbation
  - evaluation
  - benchmark design
  - objective-utility mismatch
